icant run-offs through the louvered openings in the base pan.)>>endobj1613 0 obj<</D(G1513679)/S/GoTo>>endobj1608 0 obj<</D(G1513678)/S/GoTo>>endobj1598 0 obj<</D(G1513687)/S/GoTo>>endobj1599 0 obj<</A 1614 0 R/Next 1615 0 R/Parent 1597 0 R/Title(2. Silver brazing alloy is used on copper-to-brass, copper-to-steel, or copper-to-copper. Flux is required when using silver brazing alloy. Do not use low temperature solder.)>>endobj1600 0 obj<</A 1616 0 R/Parent 1597 0 R/Prev 1615 0 R/Title(4. Brazing temperature of copper is proper when it is heated to a minimum temperature of 800°F and it is a dull red color in appearance.)>>endobj1616 0 obj<</D(G1513692)/S/GoTo>>endobj1615 0 obj<</A 1617 0 R/Next 1600 0 R/Parent 1597 0 R/Prev 1599 0 R/Title(3. Fluxes should be used carefully. Avoid excessive application and do not allow fluxes to enter into the system.)>>endobj1617 0 obj<</D(G1513691)/S/GoTo>>endobj1614 0 obj<</D(G1513690)/S/GoTo>>endobj1593 0 obj<</D(G1513709)/S/GoTo>>endobj1594 0 obj<</A 1618 0 R/Next 1619 0 R/Parent 1588 0 R/Title(a. Joint must be free of oil, grease, rust, corrosion, and refrigerant.)>>endobj1595 0 obj<</A 1620 0 R/Parent 1588 0 R/Prev 1621 0 R/Title(9. If reheating is necessary, let joint cool, wire brush, reapply flux. Reheat joint so flux melts and reapply braze material.)>>endobj1620 0 obj<</D(G1513720)/S/GoTo>>endobj1621 0 obj<</A 1622 0 R/Next 1595 0 R/Parent 1588 0 R/Prev 1623 0 R/Title(8. It is best to repair the area the first time. Reheating can cause failure to repair the area.)>>endobj1622 0 obj<</D(G1513719)/S/GoTo>>endobj1623 0 obj<</A 1624 0 R/Next 1621 0 R/Parent 1588 0 R/Prev 1625 0 R/Title(7. Once the alloy melts on the parent metal add alloy to repair the area. Maintain joint temperature until repair is complete. Do not over heat. \(withdraw torch as required\))>>endobj1624 0 obj<</D(G1513718)/S/GoTo>>endobj1625 0 obj<</A 1626 0 R/Next 1623 0 R/Parent 1588 0 R/Prev 1627 0 R/Ti